  "answer": "Your recent transactions show two EUR 240.00 card charges to **TechMart Online**, both settled:\n\n- **TX-0402**, 2026-07-14, EUR 240.00\n- **TX-0401**, 2026-07-20, EUR 240.00\n\nBefore I open anything, I need you to confirm two things:\n\n1. **Which charge is the one where the goods were not received?** I don't have a confirmed transaction ID from our earlier discussion, so please tell me which one (TX-0402 or TX-0401), or whether it's a different transaction.\n2. **Reason code.** Earlier I suggested service_not_rendered, but that code is for services. For paid goods that never arrived, **goods_not_received** is the better fit. Since the charges are identical, duplicate_charge could also apply if you were billed twice for one order. Tell me which situation matches.\n\nOnce you confirm the transaction and reason, I'll run the eligibility check. I will only open the dispute if that check passes, and I'll ask you to confirm again before filing, because a dispute cannot be reversed once submitted.",
